Command:
  bun test packages/senpi-task/src/team/member-revival.test.ts -t 'died unexpectedly'

Result:
  RED (exit 1).

Expected:
  a completed but still-resident team member whose process died unexpectedly becomes `lost` when
  reattach is disabled.

Received:
  two duplicate `deferred:reattach_disabled` outcomes, with the record silently converted from
  `resident` to `rpc_detached` while status remained `completed`.

Why this matters:
  completed is a turn result, not proof that a resident team member process still exists. Deliberate
  session shutdown pre-suspends members as `persisted_only`; an unsuspended resident with a dead PID is
  a crash and must produce an abnormal liveness state.
